###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The paper calls its on-the-fly models GAP (refs. 59, 61, 62, 67) and trains them with VASP DFT and Bayesian error estimates; it does not name the VASP machine-learned force field, so they are encoded under GAP, not VASP-MLFF. GAP training-set sizes are given only as 'roughly 600' DFT calls.
# - MACE models fine-tuned on 200 and 2,000 AIMD snapshots and on 200 foundation-model snapshots, and the S1 GAP, appear only in NEB curves (Fig. 1); they are not encoded as runs.
# - NEB barriers (e.g. 0.80 eV vs. DFT 0.83 eV), RDFs, MSDs, jump rates and vacancy formation energies are property comparisons and are not encoded. The AIMD cost estimate (about 40 days for 100 ps) is a DFT cost, not an MLIP timing.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/flototto2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

